@page
@{ViewData["Title"]="Availability and release limitations"; ViewData["Description"]="Requests are pending until an owner confirms. External bookings are manual, and confirmation email depends on configured delivery; no payments or channel management.";}
<h1>Clear requests. Clear boundaries.</h1><section class="card"><h2>A request is not a confirmed booking</h2><p>Pending requests do not hold inventory. Multiple guests may request the same dates. An owner agrees the price and property terms directly, then confirms. Confirmation rechecks dates atomically; overlapping confirmed stays or hard blocks for the same unit cannot be committed within this system.</p><p>A June 10–12 stay occupies the nights of June 10 and 11. A June 12 arrival is allowed with same-day turnover, or blocked if a one-night turnover gap is configured. Dates belong to the property's local time zone.</p><p>We cannot know bookings made elsewhere. Owners must record them before confirming. This is not a channel manager, full PMS or guarantee against all double bookings.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Accommodation prices belong on your website</h2><p>Property owners are expected to publish accommodation prices on their own website before installing the widget. Guests refer to that website and agree the final total and terms directly with the property before confirmation. StayWidget does not calculate a guest price quote. StayWidget subscription plans are separate from accommodation prices.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Communication and delivery responsibilities</h2><p>Guests save the private status link and contact the property by phone when needed. Owners check the dashboard daily, maintain outside availability and communicate price and decisions. Pending requests expire at the earlier of 48 hours or arrival-day midnight in property time. Guests may withdraw pending requests or ask to cancel confirmed stays. Only an owner cancellation releases confirmed dates.</p><p>No automatic quote, online payment, Gmail access, external calendar synchronization, travel insurance or booking protection. No sensitive guest questionnaires or uploads.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Local preview</h2><p>Not ready for live bookings. Complete Google login, actual published builder installs, operator/privacy facts, production hosting, restore and incident checks must be verified before launch. No contractual uptime or personal support SLA is offered. Mandatory rights and obligations remain applicable.</p><p>Owners should keep private booking exports and another practical contact/calendar method for outages. The service operator still has unavoidable security, backup, monitoring and recovery responsibilities.</p></section>
